# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public-repo policy: track ONLY the rendered chapter PDFs and the writing
# source that builds them. Everything else stays local: figures (baked into
# the PDFs anyway; the matplotlib ones are rebuilt by gen_figs.py), the
# applied-session Code/ and Data/ folders, build intermediates, local tooling.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1) ignore everything by default
*

# 2) but descend into sub-directories so the allow-list below can match
!*/

# 3) allow the writing source + rendered PDFs + repo essentials
!**/*.qmd
!**/preamble.tex
!**/*.bib
!**/gen_figs.py
!**/Lecture/*.pdf
!README.md
!.nojekyll
!.gitignore

# 4) ...except this stray non-chapter PDF
Basic/Lecture/02_randomization.pdf

# 5) TD folders stay local: the .qmd embeds the corrigé, and the TD PDFs are handed
#    to students via e-learn, not via the public Pages site. (Publishing a TD subject
#    is a deliberate, per-file decision — un-ignore it explicitly if you want that.)
**/TD/**

# 6) archived material (retired chapters, one-off migration scripts) never goes public
_archive/**
